   "daf": "9b",
   "sentenceId": 12,
   "he": "רַבִּי שִׁמְעוֹן בֶּן מְנַסְיָא אוֹמֵר: אֵי זֶה הוּא ״מְעֻוָּת לֹא יוּכַל לִתְקוֹן״ — זֶה הַבָּא עַל הָעֶרְוָה וְהוֹלִיד מִמֶּנָּה מַמְזֵר וְכוּ׳. הוֹלִיד — אִין, לֹא הוֹלִיד — לָא?",
   "en": "§ The mishna taught that «Rabbi Shimon ben Menasya says: Who is» the «crooked that cannot be made straight? This» verse is referring to «one who engaged in intercourse with a woman forbidden to him and fathered a mamzer with her.» The Gemara infers from the mishna: If «he fathers a child, yes,» this verse applies, as he cannot remedy the situation; if «he does not father a child, no,» the verse does not apply, as he can make amends."
  }
